      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Picture 1> is the first frame of [Shot 1]. <Subject 1> is the primary subject in <Picture 1>. <Audio 1> is the synchronized vocal and musical track performed by <Subject 1> (S1).\n\nsummary:\n[keyframe completion + audio reuse] The target video begins from <Picture 1> and shows <Subject 1> performing, using <Audio 1> as the complete final audio track. The shot maintains the exact initial camera distance, scale, and framing of <Picture 1> throughout.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Picture 1> ([Shot 1] first frame): fully_preserved - strict spatial lock.\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - <Subject 1>'s spatial footprint, relative size within the frame, visual identity, attire, and posture match <Picture 1> exactly.\n<Audio 1>: fully_copy - <Audio 1> is reused 1:1 as the target video's complete final audio track.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] The shot begins from <Picture 1> with a completely static camera rig. The camera position, field of view (FOV), focal length, and subject-to-frame ratio are permanently locked to match <Picture 1>. <Subject 1> (S1) sings with synchronized lip articulation matching <Audio 1>. <Subject 1> performs naturally with head sways and subtle body movements.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nThe copied audio track from <Audio 1> serves as the complete audio signal.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\n<Audio 1> is directly reused as the complete musical backing and audience-only score.",
